window.WOLFIE_CONTEXT_PACKS=(window.WOLFIE_CONTEXT_PACKS||[]).concat([{"id":"mission-v2-026","day":26,"level":"A2","title":"Donating clothes in good condition","ru":"Передача одежды в благотворительный магазин","goal":"Описывать состояние вещей, количество и отличия с this/that/these/those и one/ones.","version":1,"profile":"extended-v1","quality":"authored-not-independently-reviewed","grammar":{"title":"Demonstratives and one / ones","rule":"This/that используются с единственным числом; these/those — с множественным. One/ones заменяют исчисляемые существительные, чтобы не повторять их.","pattern":"This jacket / those shoes / the blue one / the smaller ones","example":"These shirts are clean, but those ones need washing.","pitfall":"Не говори this shoes: these shoes.","exercises":[["choice","___ trousers are in good condition.",["This","These","That"],1,"Trousers употребляется во множественном числе."],["type","Complete: I like the red jacket, not the blue ___.",["one"],"One replaces singular jacket."],["order","Скажи, что эти рубашки чистые.",["clean","are","shirts","These"],"These shirts are clean","These + plural noun."],["choice","Which bags should we take? The smaller ___.",["some of one","one","ones"],2,"Ones replaces plural bags."],["type","Complete: ___ coat over there needs a new button. Use this or that.",["that"],"That refers to a distant singular object."],["order","Скажи, что те ботинки слишком маленькие.",["small","too","are","boots","Those"],"Those boots are too small","Those + plural noun."]]},"words":[["a charity shop","благотворительный магазин"],["a donation bag","пакет с пожертвованиями"],["a winter coat","зимнее пальто"],["a missing button","отсутствующая пуговица"],["a small stain","небольшое пятно"],["a clothing rail","стойка для одежды"],["a collection box","коробка для сбора вещей"],["a pair of boots","пара ботинок"],["good condition","хорошее состояние"],["a donation receipt","квитанция о передаче пожертвования"]],"phrases":[["These clothes are clean and ready to donate.","Эта одежда чистая и готова к передаче."],["That coat needs a new button.","На том пальто нужна новая пуговица."],["Do you accept shoes in good condition?","Вы принимаете обувь в хорошем состоянии?"],["The smaller ones are in this bag.","Те, что поменьше, в этом пакете."],["I'll check your opening hours before I come.","Проверю часы работы, прежде чем приду."],["Are there any items you cannot accept?","Есть вещи, которые вы не принимаете?"],["I can bring the bags on Saturday morning.","Могу принести пакеты в субботу утром."],["This jacket has a small stain.","На этой куртке есть небольшое пятно."],["Let's keep the damaged items separate.","Давай отложим повреждённые вещи отдельно."],["Thanks for letting me know what is useful.","Спасибо, что сообщили, какие вещи пригодятся."]],"reading":{"title":"Donating clothes in good condition","paragraphs":["Alex is clearing out a wardrobe before winter. He finds several shirts, a coat that no longer fits and two pairs of boots. He wants to donate items that somebody else can use, so he checks each one carefully. The shirts are clean and in good condition. One coat has a missing button, and one pair of boots has a broken zip.","Alex calls a local charity shop before carrying the bags there. The volunteer explains that the shop can accept clean clothing and shoes in usable condition but cannot repair damaged items. Alex puts the clean shirts and the better pair of boots in one bag. He keeps the coat at home until he can replace the button. On Saturday morning he delivers the bag and thanks the volunteer for explaining the requirements clearly."],"questions":[["Why is Alex clearing the wardrobe?",["To find a passport","Before winter","To open a restaurant"],1],["What is wrong with one coat?",["A button is missing","It has no label","It is wet"],0],["Which items can the shop accept?",["All damaged shoes","Only new furniture","Clean usable clothing and shoes"],2],["When does Alex bring the bag?",["Friday night","Saturday morning","Monday evening"],1]]},"dialogue":[["Alex","Hello. I'm sorting some clothes at home, and I'd like to donate a bag on Saturday if you're accepting donations.","Здравствуйте. Я разбираю одежду дома и хотел бы принести пакет в субботу, если вы принимаете пожертвования."],["Volunteer","Yes, we are. Please make sure the items are clean and in good condition. What are you planning to bring?","Да, принимаем. Убедитесь, что вещи чистые и в хорошем состоянии. Что собираетесь принести?"],["Alex","These shirts are fine, and I have two pairs of boots. The smaller ones have a broken zip, though.","Эти рубашки в порядке, и есть две пары ботинок. Но у тех, что поменьше, сломана молния."],["Volunteer","We can accept the usable pair, but we don't have facilities to repair the damaged ones.","Можем принять пригодную пару, но у нас нет возможности ремонтировать повреждённые вещи."],["Alex","I understand. There's also a coat with a missing button. I'll repair that one before bringing it another day.","Понимаю. Ещё есть пальто без пуговицы. Починю его и принесу в другой день."],["Volunteer","That's helpful. We're open from ten on Saturday. Please bring the bags to the collection area by the door.","Это удобно. В субботу открываемся в десять. Принесите пакеты к месту сбора у двери."],["Alex","Thank you. I'll bring the clean shirts and the usable boots this weekend, and keep the other items separate.","Спасибо. На выходных принесу чистые рубашки и пригодные ботинки, а остальные вещи отложу отдельно."],["Volunteer","Great. If you're unsure about another item in the future, just call us before making the trip.","Отлично. Если в будущем будете сомневаться насчёт другой вещи, просто позвоните перед поездкой."]],"listening":["What will Alex repair before donating later?",["A clean shirt","The collection box","The coat with a missing button"],2],"speaking":["Describe three fictional items of clothing using this, that, these and those.","Ask a charity shop which items it accepts before bringing a bag.","Explain the difference between the blue one and the blue ones.","Role-play separating usable and damaged items without making assumptions about acceptance.","Describe one household object you could give away and its condition."],"writing":["Write a message asking a charity shop about its donation requirements.","Write a short inventory separating ready-to-donate items from those needing repair.","Write four descriptions using demonstratives and two using one or ones."],"model":"These shirts are clean and in good condition. Those boots need repair. Do you accept the larger pair? I can bring the usable items on Saturday."},{"id":"mission-v2-027","day":27,"level":"A2","title":"A quieter table at a busy café","ru":"Тихий столик в кафе","goal":"Вежливо попросить изменить место, сравнить варианты и использовать polite requests.","version":1,"profile":"extended-v1","quality":"authored-not-independently-reviewed","grammar":{"title":"Would you mind / Could we","rule":"Would you mind + -ing — вежливая просьба к собеседнику. Would you mind if I/we + Past Simple — просьба о разрешении. Could we + базовый глагол — простой вариант предложения.","pattern":"Would you mind moving the chair? / Would you mind if we sat there? / Could we move?","example":"Could we sit somewhere quieter, please?","pitfall":"Не говори Would you mind to move? Используй moving.","exercises":[["choice","Would you mind ___ the music down?",["turning","to turn","turn"],0,"Would you mind + -ing."],["type","Complete: Could we ___ (sit) near the window?",["sit"],"Could + base verb."],["order","Попроси разрешения пересесть.",["table","another","to","move","we","Could"],"Could we move to another table","Could we + move."],["choice","Choose a polite request.",["Would you mind closing the door?","Would you mind to close the door?","Would you mind closed the door?"],0,"Mind + gerund."],["type","Complete: Would you mind if we ___ (sit) outside?",["sat"],"Would you mind if + Past Simple."],["order","Спроси, свободен ли столик.",["now","available","table","that","Is"],"Is that table available now","Is + subject."]]},"words":[["a quiet table","тихий столик"],["a corner seat","место в углу"],["a table reservation","бронь столика"],["a menu stand","подставка для меню"],["a crowded café","переполненное кафе"],["a background conversation","разговор на заднем плане"],["an outdoor terrace","открытая терраса"],["a free seat","свободное место"],["a lunch rush","обеденный наплыв посетителей"],["a waiting list","лист ожидания"]],"phrases":[["Could we sit somewhere quieter, please?","Можем сесть где-нибудь потише?"],["Would you mind moving this chair a little?","Не могли бы вы немного передвинуть этот стул?"],["Is the table in the corner available?","Столик в углу свободен?"],["It's difficult to hear each other here.","Здесь трудно слышать друг друга."],["We don't mind waiting a few minutes.","Мы не против подождать несколько минут."],["The terrace is a little quieter today.","На террасе сегодня немного тише."],["We'd prefer to stay inside if possible.","Мы предпочли бы остаться внутри, если возможно."],["Could you let us know when a table is free?","Сообщите, когда освободится столик?"],["We'll keep our original seats for now.","Пока останемся на своих местах."],["Thank you for finding another option.","Спасибо, что нашли другой вариант."]],"reading":{"title":"A quieter table at a busy café","paragraphs":["Julia meets her colleague Noah in a café during the lunch rush. They want to talk about a language course, but the table they are given is close to a busy entrance. People keep walking past, and the music makes it difficult to hear each other. Julia asks the server whether they can move to a quieter place. She explains the problem without complaining about other customers.","The server says that the corner table is reserved for another group, but a small table near the window may be free in ten minutes. Julia and Noah decide to wait at their original table and order drinks. When the window table becomes available, the server helps them move. They continue their conversation in a more comfortable place. Julia thanks the server for offering a practical alternative rather than promising a table that was not available."],"questions":[["Why is the first table uncomfortable?",["It is near a busy entrance","It is outside in the snow","It has no chairs"],0],["Why can't they use the corner table?",["The café is closing","It is broken","It is reserved"],2],["When may the window table be free?",["In an hour","In ten minutes","Tomorrow"],1],["What do they do while waiting?",["Order drinks at their original table","Leave without telling anyone","Move to the reserved table"],0]]},"dialogue":[["Julia","Excuse me. Could we sit somewhere quieter, please? It's quite difficult for us to hear each other at this table.","Извините. Можем сесть где-нибудь потише? За этим столиком нам довольно трудно слышать друг друга."],["Server","I understand. The corner table is reserved, but the small table near the window should be free in about ten minutes.","Понимаю. Столик в углу забронирован, но маленький столик у окна должен освободиться примерно через десять минут."],["Noah","We don't mind waiting. Would you mind letting us know when the other customers have left?","Мы не против подождать. Сообщите, когда другие посетители уйдут?"],["Server","Of course. There's also a free table outside on the terrace if you would prefer to move straight away.","Конечно. Ещё есть свободный столик снаружи на террасе, если хотите пересесть сразу."],["Julia","Thanks, but we'd prefer to stay inside because it's a little cold today. The window table sounds good.","Спасибо, но лучше останемся внутри, потому что сегодня прохладно. Столик у окна подходит."],["Server","No problem. You can order your drinks here, and I'll help you move when the table is ready.","Без проблем. Закажите напитки здесь, а когда столик будет готов, помогу пересесть."],["Noah","That would be very helpful. We'll keep these seats for now and wait for your message.","Это очень удобно. Пока останемся здесь и будем ждать вашего сообщения."],["Server","Certainly. I'll come over as soon as the table is available. Thanks for your patience during the lunch rush.","Конечно. Подойду, как только столик освободится. Спасибо за терпение в обеденный час."]],"listening":["Where would they prefer to wait for a table?",["At another café","Inside","Outside on the terrace"],1],"speaking":["Ask for a quieter table and give a brief reason without blaming other guests.","Compare two seating options and explain which you prefer.","Use would you mind with two different actions and could we with two suggestions.","Role-play a server offering a realistic alternative when a requested table is unavailable.","Agree a waiting time and confirm what you will do until the table is ready."],"writing":["Write a polite request to a café about a quieter reserved table.","Write a reply offering two alternative seating arrangements.","Write a short review describing a service problem and how it was resolved."],"model":"Could we sit somewhere quieter, please? We don't mind waiting a few minutes. We'd prefer to stay inside if possible."},{"id":"mission-v2-028","day":28,"level":"A2","title":"Checking in at a health centre reception","ru":"Регистрация на приём в поликлинике","goal":"Уточнить время и административные требования к записи с indirect questions (базовый уровень).","version":1,"profile":"extended-v1","quality":"authored-not-independently-reviewed","grammar":{"title":"Polite indirect questions","rule":"После Could you tell me / Do you know в косвенном вопросе используется прямой порядок слов: where the room is. Для вопроса да/нет можно использовать if или whether.","pattern":"Where is the room? / Could you tell me where the room is?","example":"Could you tell me whether I need a form?","pitfall":"Не говори Could you tell me where is the room? Внутри нужен прямой порядок.","exercises":[["choice","Could you tell me where ___?",["does reception is","is reception","reception is"],2,"Indirect question: subject before verb."],["type","Complete: Do you know what time the appointment ___ (start)?",["starts"],"Subject + verb in an indirect question."],["order","Вежливо спроси, где находится стойка.",["is","reception","where","me","tell","you","Could"],"Could you tell me where reception is","Where + subject + verb."],["choice","Choose the correct question.",["Do you know if do I need a form?","Do you know I if need a form?","Do you know if I need a form?"],2,"If + subject + verb."],["type","Complete: Could you tell me which room I ___ (need)?",["need"],"I need, not do I need."],["order","Спроси, нужно ли подождать здесь.",["here","wait","should","I","if","me","tell","you","Could"],"Could you tell me if I should wait here","If + I should wait."]]},"words":[["a health centre","медицинский центр"],["a check-in desk","стойка регистрации"],["an appointment letter","письмо с записью на приём"],["a patient form","анкета пациента"],["a waiting room","зал ожидания"],["a room number","номер кабинета"],["an appointment reference","номер записи"],["an identity document","удостоверение личности"],["a reception queue","очередь на регистрацию"],["a check-in time","время регистрации"]],"phrases":[["I'm here for a booked appointment.","Я пришёл на назначенный приём."],["Could you tell me where reception is?","Подскажите, где регистратура?"],["Do you know if I need to fill in this form?","Знаете, нужно ли заполнить эту анкету?"],["Here's my appointment reference.","Вот номер моей записи."],["Which waiting room should I use?","В каком зале ожидания мне ждать?"],["Could you confirm the room number?","Можете подтвердить номер кабинета?"],["I'll wait until my number is called.","Подожду, пока вызовут мой номер."],["I arrived a little early for my appointment.","Я пришёл немного раньше назначенного времени."],["Do I need to show this document here?","Мне нужно показать этот документ здесь?"],["Thank you for explaining where to go.","Спасибо, что объяснили, куда идти."]],"reading":{"title":"Checking in at a health centre reception","paragraphs":["George arrives at a health centre fifteen minutes before a scheduled appointment. The building is new to him, and he sees two reception desks near the entrance. One desk is for general information, while the other is for people with booked appointments. He asks a staff member where he should check in and shows the appointment reference from his letter.","The receptionist finds the booking and explains that George needs to fill in a short administrative form before waiting. She points him towards a quieter waiting room on the same floor. George checks the room number because the corridor has two similar signs. He fills in the form, returns it to reception and waits for his number to be called. He is glad that he arrived early enough to ask questions without rushing. The visit is about communication and check-in, not medical advice."],"questions":[["How early does George arrive?",["Two hours","Five minutes after the appointment","Fifteen minutes"],2],["What does he show at reception?",["A restaurant menu","An appointment reference","A bus ticket"],1],["What does he need to fill in?",["An administrative form","A shopping list","A library card"],0],["Why does he check the room number?",["He wants to choose another doctor","The building is closed","Two signs look similar"],2]]},"dialogue":[["George","Good morning. I'm here for a booked appointment, but there are two reception desks. Could you tell me which one I need?","Доброе утро. Я пришёл на назначенный приём, но здесь две стойки. Подскажите, какая мне нужна?"],["Staff","The desk on the left is for booked appointments. Please have your appointment reference ready when you go there.","Стойка слева для записанных пациентов. Подготовьте номер записи, когда будете подходить."],["George","Thank you. Here's my appointment letter. Do you know if I need to fill in a form before waiting?","Спасибо. Вот письмо с записью. Знаете, нужно ли заполнить анкету перед ожиданием?"],["Receptionist","Yes, just this short administrative form. Please return it to me when you've finished, then wait in room twelve.","Да, только эту короткую административную анкету. Верните её мне, когда закончите, затем ждите в комнате двенадцать."],["George","Could you tell me where room twelve is? I can see two similar signs at the end of the corridor.","Подскажите, где комната двенадцать? В конце коридора вижу две похожие таблички."],["Receptionist","It's the second door on the right, just after the noticeboard. Your number will be called from there.","Это вторая дверь справа, сразу после доски объявлений. Ваш номер вызовут оттуда."],["George","All right. I'll complete the form and bring it back before I go to the waiting room. Thanks for your help.","Хорошо. Заполню анкету и верну её, прежде чем идти в зал ожидания. Спасибо за помощь."],["Receptionist","You're welcome. If the directions are unclear, just ask again at the desk. There's no need to rush.","Пожалуйста. Если указания непонятны, просто спросите ещё раз у стойки. Спешить не нужно."]],"listening":["Where is room twelve?",["Second door on the right","First door on the left","Outside the building"],0],"speaking":["Ask where to check in for a fictional appointment without giving real personal information.","Turn three direct questions about opening times, rooms and forms into polite indirect questions.","Confirm a room number and repeat directions back to a staff member.","Role-play explaining that you have arrived early and asking what administrative step comes next.","Describe a fictional waiting-room visit in sequence without discussing medical treatment."],"writing":["Write a message asking a health centre to confirm an appointment time and check-in location.","Write a clear set of administrative directions for a fictional visitor.","Write five indirect questions about a public service desk."],"model":"I'm here for a booked appointment. Could you tell me where I should check in? Do you know if I need to fill in a form? Thank you."},{"id":"mission-v2-029","day":29,"level":"A2","title":"Arranging a board-game evening","ru":"Вечер настольных игр","goal":"Согласовать время, предпочтения и правила с suggestions: let's, shall we, how about.","version":1,"profile":"extended-v1","quality":"authored-not-independently-reviewed","grammar":{"title":"Suggestions and invitations","rule":"Let's + базовый глагол, Shall we + базовый глагол и How about + существительное или -ing помогают предложить совместное действие. Would you like to + глагол — приглашение.","pattern":"Let's play. / Shall we start at seven? / How about trying a new game?","example":"How about starting with a short game?","pitfall":"Не говори How about to play? Правильно: How about playing?","exercises":[["choice","How about ___ a short game first?",["play","playing","to play"],1,"How about + -ing."],["type","Complete: Let's ___ (choose) a game together.",["choose"],"Let's + base verb."],["order","Предложи начать в семь.",["seven","at","start","we","Shall"],"Shall we start at seven","Shall we + base verb."],["choice","Choose a natural invitation.",["Would you to like join us?","Would you like to join us?","Would you like join us?"],1,"Would you like to + verb."],["type","Complete: How about ___ (bring) a snack?",["bringing"],"How about + -ing."],["order","Предложи сначала объяснить правила.",["first","rules","the","explain","us","Let"],"Let us explain the rules first","Let us + base verb."]]},"words":[["a board game","настольная игра"],["a game piece","игровая фишка"],["a set of rules","набор правил"],["a dice roll","бросок игральной кости"],["a score sheet","лист подсчёта очков"],["a practice round","пробный раунд"],["a team game","командная игра"],["a player turn","ход игрока"],["a game box","коробка с игрой"],["a beginner-friendly game","игра, подходящая новичкам"]],"phrases":[["How about playing a short game first?","Как насчёт сначала сыграть в короткую игру?"],["Shall we start at seven?","Начнём в семь?"],["Let's explain the rules before we begin.","Давай объясним правила перед началом."],["Would you like to join our team?","Хочешь присоединиться к нашей команде?"],["You can have the next turn.","Можешь ходить следующим."],["I haven't played this game before.","Я раньше не играл в эту игру."],["Could we try a practice round?","Можем попробовать пробный раунд?"],["Let's choose something everyone can enjoy.","Давай выберем то, что понравится всем."],["We can stop after one more round.","Можем закончить после ещё одного раунда."],["Thanks for explaining that rule clearly.","Спасибо, что понятно объяснил это правило."]],"reading":{"title":"Arranging a board-game evening","paragraphs":["Four friends are planning a board-game evening at Mia's flat. Two of them enjoy long strategy games, while the others have never played that type of game. Mia wants everyone to feel comfortable, so she suggests starting with a shorter team game. She sends a message asking whether seven o'clock is a good starting time and whether anybody would like to bring a snack.","When the friends arrive, Mia shows them two possible games. They choose the one with simpler rules and agree to play a practice round without keeping score. During the first round, one player forgets whose turn comes next. Another friend explains the rule calmly, and they continue. After an hour they decide to play one more round and then finish. Everybody has taken part, and the group plans to try a more difficult game another time."],"questions":[["How many friends are planning the evening?",["Six","Four","Two"],1],["Why does Mia suggest a short game?",["Some friends are beginners","She has lost the rules","She wants to leave immediately"],0],["What do they do during the practice round?",["Play for money","Keep a formal score","Play without keeping score"],2],["What do they decide after an hour?",["Start an unrelated event","Play one more round and finish","Stay until morning"],1]]},"dialogue":[["Mia","I'm thinking of having a board-game evening on Friday. Would you like to join us at about seven o'clock?","Думаю устроить вечер настольных игр в пятницу. Хочешь присоединиться примерно в семь?"],["Chris","Yes, I'd love to. I haven't played many board games, though. Are we going to start with something quite easy?","Да, с удовольствием. Правда, я мало играл в настольные игры. Начнём с чего-нибудь довольно простого?"],["Mia","Of course. How about trying a short team game first? We can explain the rules and play a practice round.","Конечно. Как насчёт сначала попробовать короткую командную игру? Объясним правила и сыграем пробный раунд."],["Chris","That sounds good. Shall we keep score during the first round, or can we just learn how it works?","Звучит хорошо. Будем считать очки в первом раунде или просто разберёмся, как играть?"],["Mia","Let's play without keeping score at first. Once everyone understands the rules, we can start the real game.","Давай сначала сыграем без подсчёта очков. Когда все поймут правила, начнём настоящую игру."],["Chris","Great. How about bringing some snacks as well? I can pick up something on my way after work.","Отлично. Как насчёт закусок? Могу купить что-нибудь по дороге после работы."],["Mia","Thanks, that's kind of you. We can stop after a couple of rounds if anybody needs to leave early.","Спасибо, это любезно. Можем закончить после пары раундов, если кому-нибудь нужно уйти пораньше."],["Chris","Perfect. I'll be there around seven. Please send me the address privately before Friday.","Отлично. Буду примерно в семь. Пришли мне адрес лично до пятницы."]],"listening":["What will they do during the first round?",["Play a tournament","Invite strangers","Play without keeping score"],2],"speaking":["Invite a friend to a fictional game evening and offer two possible starting times.","Make three suggestions using let's, shall we and how about.","Explain the rules of a simple game in five short instructions.","Role-play helping a beginner who has misunderstood a rule.","Suggest ending an activity at a mutually convenient time and confirm agreement."],"writing":["Write a friendly group invitation with the time and beginner-friendly plan.","Write five simple game instructions with a polite reminder about turns.","Write a short message proposing an alternative game if the first one is too difficult."],"model":"Would you like to join our game evening? How about starting with a short game? Let's play a practice round before keeping score."},{"id":"mission-v2-030","day":30,"level":"A2","title":"Changing an internet service appointment","ru":"Изменение визита специалиста по интернету","goal":"Итоговая бытовая практика: сообщить проблему, уточнить детали, изменить запись и подтвердить договорённость.","version":1,"profile":"extended-v1","quality":"authored-not-independently-reviewed","grammar":{"title":"Integrated A2 review: questions, past events, plans","rule":"Для прошлых событий используй Past Simple; после did — базовая форма. Для просьбы используй could + базовый глагол. Заранее выбранный план можно описать going to.","pattern":"It stopped yesterday. / Could you check the booking? / I'm going to be home after four.","example":"I called yesterday, but I need to change the appointment.","pitfall":"Не смешивай вспомогательные глаголы: Did you call?, не Did you called?","exercises":[["choice","The connection ___ working last night.",["stopped","stop","has stopped"],0,"Last night — finished past time."],["type","Complete: Did you ___ (receive) my message?",["receive"],"After did use base form."],["order","Вежливо попроси проверить запись.",["please","appointment","my","check","you","Could"],"Could you check my appointment please","Could + base verb."],["choice","I'm ___ be at home after four.",["going to","go to","going"],0,"Be going to + verb."],["type","Complete: The visit is ___ Monday. Use in, on or at.",["on"],"On + day."],["order","Скажи, что отправишь подтверждение сейчас.",["now","confirmation","the","send","will","I"],"I will send the confirmation now","Will + base verb."]]},"words":[["a service appointment","запись на обслуживание"],["a home internet connection","домашнее интернет-соединение"],["a support reference","номер обращения в поддержку"],["a service provider","поставщик услуг"],["a connection problem","проблема с соединением"],["a booking confirmation","подтверждение записи"],["an alternative date","альтернативная дата"],["a rescheduling request","запрос на перенос записи"],["a contact number","контактный номер"],["an appointment record","запись о назначенном визите"]],"phrases":[["The connection stopped working last night.","Соединение перестало работать прошлой ночью."],["I reported the problem yesterday.","Я сообщил о проблеме вчера."],["Could you check my service appointment?","Можете проверить запись на обслуживание?"],["I'm not going to be home before four.","Я буду дома только после четырёх."],["Is there another appointment available on Monday?","Есть другое свободное время в понедельник?"],["Please keep the original support reference.","Пожалуйста, сохраните исходный номер обращения."],["Could you confirm the new time in writing?","Можете подтвердить новое время письменно?"],["I'll let you know if anything changes.","Сообщу, если что-нибудь изменится."],["The appointment has been moved to Tuesday.","Запись перенесена на вторник."],["Thank you for explaining the next step.","Спасибо, что объяснили следующий шаг."]],"reading":{"title":"Changing an internet service appointment","paragraphs":["Amina has a home internet problem and contacts her service provider on Wednesday evening. The support agent records the problem and offers an appointment on Friday morning. Amina agrees at first, but the next day her work schedule changes. She cannot be at home until four on Friday and needs to ask for a different visit time.","She calls the service provider again and gives the original support reference instead of starting a new request. The agent checks the record and explains that Friday afternoon is fully booked. A visit is available on Monday between four and six. Amina checks her calendar, agrees to the new time and asks for written confirmation. When the message arrives, she checks the address, date and time. She keeps the reference number and knows how to contact the provider if the plan changes again."],"questions":[["When does Amina first contact support?",["Wednesday evening","Friday morning","Monday afternoon"],0],["Why must she change the appointment?",["She moves to another town","The internet is already fixed","Her work schedule changes"],2],["What new time does the agent offer?",["Tuesday at nine","Monday between four and six","Friday morning"],1],["What does she check in the confirmation?",["Address, date and time","The weather report","Her friend's email address"],0]]},"dialogue":[["Amina","Hello. I reported an internet connection problem yesterday, and I have an appointment for Friday morning. Could you check the booking for me?","Здравствуйте. Вчера сообщила о проблеме с интернетом, и на пятницу утром назначен визит. Можете проверить запись?"],["Agent","Certainly. Do you have the support reference from the original message? That will help me find the correct record.","Конечно. У вас есть номер обращения из исходного сообщения? Он поможет найти нужную запись."],["Amina","Yes, I have it here. My work schedule has changed, so I'm not going to be home before four on Friday.","Да, он у меня. График работы изменился, поэтому в пятницу до четырёх меня не будет дома."],["Agent","I see. Friday afternoon is fully booked, but we have an available visit on Monday between four and six.","Понимаю. Пятница после обеда полностью занята, но есть свободное время в понедельник с четырёх до шести."],["Amina","Monday works for me. Could you confirm the new time in writing and keep the same support reference, please?","Понедельник мне подходит. Можете подтвердить новое время письменно и сохранить прежний номер обращения?"],["Agent","Of course. I'll update the appointment record now and send a confirmation with the address, date and time.","Конечно. Сейчас обновлю запись и отправлю подтверждение с адресом, датой и временем."],["Amina","Thank you. I'll check the message when it arrives. Please let me know if the appointment needs to change again.","Спасибо. Проверю сообщение, когда оно придёт. Сообщите, если запись снова придётся изменить."],["Agent","Certainly. The new appointment is Monday between four and six. The original support reference will stay the same.","Конечно. Новый визит в понедельник с четырёх до шести. Исходный номер обращения останется прежним."]],"listening":["What stays the same after rescheduling?",["The agent's working hours","The support reference","The Friday appointment"],1],"speaking":["Report a fictional everyday service problem using a finished past time and a clear present consequence.","Ask three polite questions about an existing appointment without starting a duplicate request.","Explain why you need a new date and offer two alternatives.","Role-play confirming a new date, time window and reference number in a telephone call.","Give a one-minute summary of the original event, change of plan and agreed next step."],"writing":["Write a rescheduling request with the original booking reference, reason and two alternatives.","Write a confirmation message giving the new date and time and what remains unchanged.","Write a six-sentence account that uses Past Simple, could, going to and a time preposition."],"model":"I reported the problem yesterday. Could you check my appointment? I'm going to be at home after four on Monday. Please send the new time in writing."},{"id":"mission-v2-031","day":31,"level":"A2","title":"A ticket machine that takes only cards","ru":"Билетный автомат принимает только карты","goal":"Купить билет, описать завершённые действия и уточнить причину ошибки оплаты.","version":1,"profile":"extended-v1","quality":"authored-not-independently-reviewed","grammar":{"title":"Past Simple: regular and irregular verbs","rule":"Для завершённого действия в прошлом используй Past Simple. Правильные глаголы обычно получают -ed; формы неправильных нужно запоминать.","pattern":"I tried / I paid / I bought / I went","example":"I tried the machine twice, then I bought a ticket at the counter.","pitfall":"Не говори buyed или payed в значении оплаты: bought, paid.","exercises":[["choice","Yesterday I ___ a day pass at the station.",["buy","bought","buyed"],1,"Buy → bought."],["type","Complete: I ___ (try) the other machine.",["tried"],"Try → tried."],["order","Скажи: я заплатил картой у кассы.",["counter","the","at","card","by","paid","I"],"I paid by card at the counter","Pay → paid."],["choice","The machine ___ my first card ten minutes ago.",["rejects","rejected","reject"],1,"Завершённое действие: rejected."],["type","Complete: We ___ (go) to the ticket office after that.",["went"],"Go → went."],["order","Скажи: сотрудник показал мне другой автомат.",["machine","another","me","showed","clerk","The"],"The clerk showed me another machine","Show → showed."]]},"words":[["a card-only machine","автомат, принимающий только карты"],["a rejected payment","отклонённый платёж"],["a ticket slot","щель для выдачи билета"],["a payment screen","экран оплаты"],["a fare zone map","карта тарифных зон"],["a printed day pass","напечатанный проездной на день"],["a staffed ticket window","билетная касса с сотрудником"],["a contactless symbol","значок бесконтактной оплаты"],["a transaction receipt","чек по операции"],["an exact fare","точная стоимость проезда"]],"phrases":[["The machine rejected my payment twice.","Автомат дважды отклонил мой платёж."],["Does this machine take cash as well?","Этот автомат принимает и наличные?"],["I bought a printed day pass at the counter.","Я купил бумажный дневной проездной в кассе."],["The screen showed an error after I tapped my card.","После того как я приложил карту, экран показал ошибку."],["Could you point out the staffed ticket window?","Не могли бы вы показать, где касса с сотрудником?"],["I paid the same fare at the ticket office.","Я заплатил ту же стоимость в кассе."],["The ticket came out of this slot.","Билет вышел из этой щели."],["I checked the zones before I chose the ticket.","Я проверил зоны, прежде чем выбрать билет."],["Please keep the transaction receipt until you arrive.","Пожалуйста, сохраните чек до прибытия."],["I went to the platform after buying my pass.","Я пошёл на платформу после покупки проездного."]],"reading":{"title":"A ticket machine that takes only cards","paragraphs":["On Tuesday morning, Elena arrived at a station she had never used before. She needed a day pass for two fare zones because she planned to visit a museum and a friend. The first ticket machine looked simple. She chose the zones, tapped her bank card and waited, but the payment screen showed an error. She tried once more and got the same message. There was no ticket in the slot, so she did not try a third time.","Elena asked a station worker whether she could buy a pass with cash. He pointed to a staffed ticket window near the entrance. At the window, she explained what happened and asked for the same two-zone pass. The clerk checked the fare, accepted her cash and gave her a receipt. Elena kept both the pass and the receipt in her coat pocket. She reached the platform before her train arrived, and she made a note of the ticket office for her next visit."],"questions":[["How many fare zones did Elena need?",["One","Two","Three"],1],["What appeared on the payment screen?",["A map","A receipt","An error"],2],["Where did Elena finally buy her pass?",["At a staffed ticket window","On the train","At the museum"],0],["What did she keep in her coat pocket?",["Only her bank card","A pass and a receipt","A station map"],1]]},"dialogue":[["Elena","Excuse me. I tried this machine twice, but it rejected my card both times. No ticket came out.","Извините. Я дважды попробовала этот автомат, но он оба раза отклонил карту. Билет не вышел."],["Worker","This machine takes cards only. You can use the staffed ticket window near the entrance if you prefer cash.","Этот автомат принимает только карты. Если предпочитаете наличные, можете воспользоваться кассой у входа."],["Elena","I chose two fare zones because I need to visit two places today. Is a day pass suitable?","Я выбрала две тарифные зоны, потому что мне сегодня нужно посетить два места. Подойдёт дневной проездной?"],["Worker","Yes, ask for a day pass for zones one and two. The clerk will tell you the exact fare before you pay.","Да, попросите дневной проездной для первой и второй зон. Кассир назовёт точную цену до оплаты."],["Elena","Do I need to show the failed payment screen to the clerk, or can I just explain what happened?","Нужно показать кассиру экран с ошибкой оплаты или достаточно объяснить, что произошло?"],["Worker","You can explain it. If you see a charge later, keep the receipt and contact the ticket office.","Можете объяснить. Если позже увидите списание, сохраните чек и обратитесь в кассу."],["Elena","All right, I'll go to the window now. Thank you for showing me where it is.","Хорошо, сейчас пойду к кассе. Спасибо, что показали, где она находится."],["Worker","You're welcome. The platforms are straight ahead after you buy your ticket.","Пожалуйста. После покупки билета платформы прямо по ходу движения."]],"listening":["What did the worker say about paying with cash?",["Use the staffed window","Pay the driver","Put cash in the card slot"],0],"speaking":["Describe the order of Elena's actions in the Past Simple.","Explain a failed card payment to a station worker.","Ask for a day pass for two zones and confirm the fare.","Say three things you did yesterday at a station or shop.","Role-play asking where to buy a ticket without trying the same machine again."],"writing":["Write a five-sentence account of a failed ticket purchase and its solution.","Write a polite question asking whether a ticket machine accepts cash.","Write four Past Simple sentences using tried, paid, bought and went."],"model":"I tried the ticket machine twice, but my payment failed. I went to the ticket office and bought a day pass. I paid in cash and kept the receipt."},{"id":"mission-v2-041","day":41,"level":"A2","title":"Sending a registered letter","ru":"Отправка заказного письма","goal":"Отправить письмо с отслеживанием и объяснить, что сделал или не сделал на почте.","version":1,"profile":"extended-v1","quality":"authored-not-independently-reviewed","grammar":{"title":"Past Simple negatives and questions with did","rule":"Did используется для вопросов о завершённом прошлом, didn't — для отрицаний. После did/didn't глагол стоит в начальной форме.","pattern":"Did you send it? / I didn't send it.","example":"Did you keep the proof of posting? I didn't throw it away.","pitfall":"Не говори Did you sent? или didn't sent.","exercises":[["choice","Did you ___ the address before posting the letter?",["checked","check","checks"],1,"После did — check."],["type","Complete: I didn't ___ (seal) the envelope at home.",["seal"],"После didn't — seal."],["order","Спроси: ты сохранил почтовый чек?",["receipt","postal","the","keep","you","Did"],"Did you keep the postal receipt","Did + subject + base form."],["choice","I ___ write the postcode yesterday because I didn't know it.",["don't","didn't","wasn't"],1,"Отрицание Past Simple: didn't."],["type","Complete: Where did you ___ (buy) the stamps?",["buy"],"После did — buy."],["order","Скажи: я не забыл обратный адрес.",["address","return","the","forget","not","did","I"],"I did not forget the return address","Did not + forget."]]},"words":[["a proof of posting","квитанция об отправке"],["a registered letter","заказное письмо"],["a padded envelope","конверт с мягкой прокладкой"],["a postal scale","почтовые весы"],["a delivery signature","подпись при вручении"],["a handwritten postcode","почтовый индекс, написанный от руки"],["a tracking slip","квитанция с номером отслеживания"],["a postal clerk","почтовый служащий"],["a return address label","наклейка с обратным адресом"],["an unsealed envelope","незапечатанный конверт"]],"phrases":[["Did you write the postcode on the envelope?","Ты написал почтовый индекс на конверте?"],["I didn't seal the envelope until I checked the address.","Я не запечатал конверт, пока не проверил адрес."],["I'd like to send this as a registered letter.","Я хотел бы отправить это заказным письмом."],["Does the recipient need to sign for this letter?","Получатель должен расписаться за это письмо?"],["I kept the proof of posting in my wallet.","Я сохранил квитанцию об отправке в кошельке."],["Could you weigh this padded envelope, please?","Не могли бы вы взвесить этот конверт с прокладкой?"],["Where can I find the tracking number on this slip?","Где на этой квитанции номер отслеживания?"],["I didn't include any coins or loose objects.","Я не положил монеты или незакреплённые предметы."],["The clerk explained the delivery options before I paid.","Сотрудник объяснил варианты доставки до оплаты."],["I wrote my return address on the back of the envelope.","Я написал обратный адрес на обороте конверта."]],"reading":{"title":"Sending a registered letter","paragraphs":["Daniel needed to send a signed document to an office in another town. He wanted to know when the letter arrived, so he decided to ask about registered delivery. He put the document in a padded envelope but left the envelope open until he could check the full address. At the post office, he noticed that he had forgotten the postcode. He found it in the office's email and wrote it clearly beside the town name.","The postal clerk asked him whether he wanted an ordinary letter or a service with tracking. Daniel chose the tracked option and asked whether someone would sign for it. The clerk explained the service available for that destination, weighed the envelope and gave him the price. Daniel sealed the envelope, paid and received a proof of posting with a tracking number. At home, he photographed the slip so that he could find the number even if he misplaced the paper receipt."],"questions":[["Why did Daniel want tracked delivery?",["He wanted to know when the letter arrived","He wanted to send cash","He needed a larger envelope"],0],["What information had he forgotten?",["His name","The postcode","The clerk's name"],1],["What did the clerk do before giving the price?",["Opened the letter","Called the recipient","Weighed the envelope"],2],["Why did Daniel photograph the slip?",["To remember the tracking number","To advertise the post office","To read the document again"],0]]},"dialogue":[["Daniel","Good morning. I'd like to send this document as a registered letter. Is tracking available for this address?","Доброе утро. Я хотел бы отправить этот документ заказным письмом. Для этого адреса доступно отслеживание?"],["Clerk","Let me check the destination. Did you write the full postcode and your return address on the envelope?","Давайте проверю место назначения. Вы написали полный почтовый индекс и обратный адрес на конверте?"],["Daniel","Yes, I checked them just now. I didn't seal the envelope at home because I wanted to check the address first.","Да, только что проверил. Дома я не запечатал конверт, потому что сначала хотел проверить адрес."],["Clerk","Please seal it now and put it on the scale. I'll explain which delivery services are available.","Теперь запечатайте его и положите на весы. Я объясню, какие услуги доставки доступны."],["Daniel","Does the recipient need to sign when the letter arrives? I need to know that the office received it.","Получателю нужно расписаться при вручении? Мне нужно знать, что офис получил письмо."],["Clerk","For this option, you can follow the tracking information and see whether delivery was completed. Here is the price.","При этом варианте вы можете отслеживать отправление и видеть, завершена ли доставка. Вот стоимость."],["Daniel","That works for me. Could you show me where the tracking number is printed on the receipt?","Меня это устраивает. Не могли бы вы показать, где на квитанции напечатан номер отслеживания?"],["Clerk","It's printed here below the date. Keep the receipt until you have the delivery confirmation.","Он напечатан здесь под датой. Храните квитанцию до подтверждения доставки."]],"listening":["What does Daniel ask the clerk to show him?",["The office address","The tracking number on the receipt","The opening hours"],1],"speaking":["Explain why you would choose tracked delivery for an important document.","Ask five Past Simple questions about a recent visit to a post office.","Tell the clerk what information you did not write on an envelope at first.","Describe checking an address, weighing a letter and keeping a receipt.","Role-play asking whether a delivery service includes a signature."],"writing":["Write a short message telling a recipient that a document was posted and that tracking is available.","Write four did questions and four didn't answers about a fictional postal visit.","Write a checklist of address details to check before sealing a letter."],"model":"I sent the document this morning. I didn't seal the envelope until I checked the postcode. Did you receive the tracking number? I kept the proof of posting."},{"id":"mission-v2-042","day":42,"level":"A2","title":"A pair of shoes that does not fit","ru":"Обмен обуви неподходящего размера","goal":"Объяснить причину обмена, уточнить наличие размера и сравнить две пары с was/were.","version":1,"profile":"extended-v1","quality":"authored-not-independently-reviewed","grammar":{"title":"Was / were in descriptions and questions","rule":"Was употребляется с I/he/she/it, were — с you/we/they. В вопросе was/were ставятся перед подлежащим; в отрицании — wasn't/weren't.","pattern":"The size was wrong. / Were they comfortable?","example":"The shoes were too narrow, but the colour was right.","pitfall":"Не говори the shoes was: shoes — множественное число.","exercises":[["choice","The left shoe ___ comfortable, but the right one hurt.",["were","was","be"],1,"The left shoe — единственное число."],["type","Complete: Both shoes ___ too narrow yesterday.",["were"],"Both shoes — множественное число."],["order","Спроси: ботинки были удобными?",["comfortable","boots","the","Were"],"Were the boots comfortable","Were перед подлежащим."],["choice","The size label ___ missing when I opened the box.",["were","was","are"],1,"The label was."],["type","Complete: The insoles ___ (negative, past of be) damaged.",["weren't"],"Множественное число: weren't."],["order","Скажи: коробка была в хорошем состоянии.",["condition","good","in","was","box","The"],"The box was in good condition","Box — singular: was."]]},"words":[["a half-size larger","на полразмера больше"],["a narrow fitting","узкая полнота обуви"],["a size label","ярлык с размером"],["a removable insole","съёмная стелька"],["a shoe fitting bench","скамья для примерки обуви"],["a stiff heel counter","жёсткий задник обуви"],["a clean sole","чистая подошва"],["an unused replacement pair","новая пара на замену"],["an exchange desk","стойка обмена товара"],["the original shoe box","оригинальная коробка от обуви"]],"phrases":[["The shoes were too narrow across the front.","Обувь была слишком узкой в передней части."],["The colour was right, but the size wasn't.","Цвет подходил, а размер — нет."],["Do you have the same model half a size larger?","Есть такая же модель на полразмера больше?"],["I tried both shoes on indoors.","Я примерил оба ботинка в помещении."],["The soles were clean when I brought them back.","Подошвы были чистыми, когда я принёс их обратно."],["Could I try a pair with a wider fitting?","Можно примерить пару большей полноты?"],["The original box was still in good condition.","Оригинальная коробка оставалась в хорошем состоянии."],["Were these shoes part of the same exchange policy?","На эту обувь распространялись те же условия обмена?"],["The new pair was more comfortable around my toes.","Новая пара была удобнее в области пальцев."],["I'll keep the new receipt with the replacement pair.","Я сохраню новый чек вместе с парой на замену."]],"reading":{"title":"A pair of shoes that does not fit","paragraphs":["Nina bought a pair of walking shoes on Friday. The shoes looked comfortable in the shop, but she only tried them for a minute because she was in a hurry. At home, she walked around the living room for a few minutes. The left shoe was fine, but the right one was too narrow across the front. She stopped wearing the shoes and put them back into the original box with the receipt.","On Saturday she visited the exchange desk and explained the problem. The assistant checked the soles and asked whether Nina had worn the shoes outside. Nina said that she had only tried them indoors. The assistant checked the store's exchange conditions and found another pair of the same model with a wider fitting. Nina tried both shoes on slowly, stood up and walked a little. They were much more comfortable. She accepted the replacement pair and kept the new receipt."],"questions":[["When did Nina buy the shoes?",["Saturday","Friday","Sunday"],1],["Which shoe was too narrow?",["The right one","The left one","Both were too wide"],0],["Where had Nina worn the original pair?",["In a park","On a long walk","Only indoors"],2],["Why did she accept the replacement pair?",["It was a different colour","It was more comfortable","It had no box"],1]]},"dialogue":[["Nina","Hello. I bought these shoes yesterday. The colour was fine, but the right shoe was too narrow when I tried it at home.","Здравствуйте. Я купила эту обувь вчера. Цвет подходил, но правый ботинок оказался слишком узким, когда я примерила его дома."],["Assistant","Were the shoes worn outside at all, or did you only try them on indoors?","Вы носили обувь на улице или только примеряли в помещении?"],["Nina","Only indoors. The soles were clean, and I brought the original box and the receipt with me.","Только в помещении. Подошвы были чистыми, и я принесла оригинальную коробку и чек."],["Assistant","Let me check the exchange conditions. Would you prefer a larger size or the same length with a wider fitting?","Позвольте проверить условия обмена. Вы предпочитаете больший размер или ту же длину с большей полнотой?"],["Nina","The length was right. I think the wider fitting would be better, if you have one in this colour.","Длина подходила. Думаю, большая полнота будет лучше, если есть такая пара в этом цвете."],["Assistant","We have this pair. Please try both shoes on and walk around a little before deciding.","У нас есть эта пара. Пожалуйста, примерьте оба ботинка и немного пройдитесь перед решением."],["Nina","These feel much better. My toes have more space, and the heels are comfortable too.","В этой паре гораздо удобнее. Пальцам свободнее, и пятки тоже чувствуют себя комфортно."],["Assistant","Great. I'll process the exchange and give you a new receipt for the replacement pair.","Отлично. Я оформлю обмен и выдам новый чек на пару на замену."]],"listening":["What does Nina prefer for the replacement pair?",["A different colour","A wider fitting with the same length","A smaller size"],1],"speaking":["Describe the original shoes using was and were in different sentences.","Ask a shop assistant for the same model in a wider fitting.","Compare two fictional pairs by length, width and comfort.","Explain politely why you stopped wearing a pair of shoes.","Role-play an exchange and ask about the receipt and store conditions."],"writing":["Write a short explanation of a shoe-fitting problem for an exchange desk.","Write six sentences contrasting the original pair with its replacement using was/were.","Write a dialogue in which a customer asks for a wider fitting without assuming an exchange is guaranteed."],"model":"The shoes were clean, and the box was in good condition. The right shoe was too narrow. The replacement pair was more comfortable, so I accepted it."}]);
